ove $900 look like outliers and need checking."], "action_items": [{"action": "Deep-dive Segment B's order economics", "expected_impact": "Stop paying more for less revenue"}, {"action": "Review the three orders above $900", "expected_impact": "Cleaner forecasts and budgets"}]}, "analyst_view": {"methodology": "Pearson correlation on numeric pairs, one-way ANOVA across segment, month-over-month trend per segment, IQR \u00d7 3 outlier rule.", "statistical_notes": ["r(revenue, marketing_spend) = 0.570, n = 3,000", "ANOVA F on revenue by segment, p < 0.001"], "caveats": ["One month of data limits trend conclusions.", "Correlation is not causation: spend may follow expected demand."], "code_references": ["df.groupby('segment')['revenue'].mean()"]}, "additional_issues_note": "", "generated_at": "2026-10-27T12:00:00Z"}}

